  "_doc": "The energy system's species data (battle/energy.gd, design/energy_system.md). capacity: level -> energy slots (the highest key at or below the level wins; a species may shift it with capacity_shift, in slots). max_capacity: the most slots anything has. energy_types: the energy kinds, in gallery order (Normal folds into Colorless, as in the card game). type_energy: a Pokémon type -> its energy kind when the names differ. energy_names: how a kind is shown (the card game's names). species.<id>: name, types, focus (the energy kinds a turn's chips come in, in order, cycled: the first chip of every turn is focus[0]; mostly its own types, plus Colorless), wild_levels [lo, hi], learnset [{level, move}] (moves.json ids; a move can be learned once the level is reached and the bar can pay its cost; learned moves are never forgotten), ai (the wild one's default plan style: aggressive | strategic | evasive). energy_items: the hook for rare items that restore energy in battle: restore (chips), type ('' = the Pokémon's next focus kind, 'colorless', or a kind), price.",
